<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khandesh</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khandesh is a historical region in the valley of the Tapti river in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, now mainly covered by the Jalgaon, Dhule and Nandurbar districts. From the late 14th century to 1601 it was ruled by the Faruqi sultans from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burhanpur">Burhanpur</a>. It then became a Mughal province, passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> in the 18th century and was taken by the British in 1818.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khandesh.jpg" alt="Khandesh" width="320" height="174" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Huge Earth · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Purna_river_of_Muktainagar_in_Jalgaon,_Maharashtra.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
